  "question": "Can the NLC first-party digital ancient-book pages and current microfilm item records classify 411999008600/601, 113028/113029 and 00O003570/571 while preserving SYS/UID/local-call/barcode/acquisition firewalls?",
  "answer": "YES. NLC READ DATA_892 DIRECTLY RETURNS TONGHU UNDER IDENTIFIER/FID 411999008600 WITH OPEN-OBJECT BID 113028.0 AND ZHUNZHAI UNDER IDENTIFIER/FID 411999008601 WITH BID 113029.0. CURRENT NLC MICROFILM WORK RECORDS SYS 002146415 / UID UCS01003553255 AND SYS 002146416 / UID UCS01003553256 DIRECTLY EMIT STRUCTURED 905B VALUES 00O003570 AND 00O003571, WHILE THEIR 455 NOTES RECIPROCALLY STATE THAT THE COMPANION TITLE WAS SEPARATELY PHOTOGRAPHED AT THE OTHER NUMBER. MULTIPLE INSTITUTIONAL CNMARC CONTROLS DEFINE 905B AS 登录号 / REGISTRATION-ACCESSION NUMBER. THEREFORE 00O003570/571 ARE CLASSIFIED AS THE MICROFILM OBJECT REGISTRATION/LOGIN-NUMBER PAIR, NOT THE ORIGINAL RARE-BOOK CALL NUMBERS, BARCODES OR HISTORICAL QU ACQUISITION/DONATION NUMBERS. 455 EMBEDDED 001 VALUES 411999008600/601 ARE DIRECTLY CROSS-BOUND TO ACTIVE NLC READ DATA_892 FIDS FOR THE CORRESPONDING DIGITIZED ANCIENT-BOOK RESOURCES. CURRENT META BIBLIOGRAPHIC SYS/UID, RARE-BOOK 905S LOCAL CALL NUMBERS, DIGITAL FIDS/BIDS AND MICROFILM 905B REGISTRATION NUMBERS REMAIN DISTINCT IDENTIFIER LAYERS.",
